## Problem

`BlockMutator::MAX_BLOCK_DEPTH` (32) is **not enforced on the write path** of `edit-block-tree`. The depth validator `BlockMutator::validate_tree_depth()` is only called from `BlockReferences::assign_refs()` — i.e. when **reading** a post via `get-page-blocks` — so an agent can freely insert a 33+ level nested tree via `insert-child`, `replace-block`, or `wrap-in-group` and the cap is silently bypassed.

## Repro

```php
wp_set_current_user(get_user_by('login', 'admin')->ID);

$first_ref = wp_get_ability('sd-ai-agent/get-page-blocks')
  ->execute(['post_id' => 156])['blocks'][0]['ref'];

// Build a 33-deep group tree
$deep = ['blockName' => 'core/group', 'attrs' => [], 'innerHTML' => '', 'innerBlocks' => []];
for ($i = 0; $i < 32; $i++) {
  $deep = ['blockName' => 'core/group', 'attrs' => [], 'innerHTML' => '', 'innerBlocks' => [$deep]];
}

$r = wp_get_ability('sd-ai-agent/edit-block-tree')->execute([
  'post_id'   => 156,
  'op'        => 'insert-child',
  'ref'       => $first_ref,
  'block_def' => $deep,
]);

// EXPECTED: WP_Error('block_depth_exceeded')
// ACTUAL:   success=true (cap bypassed)
```

## Evidence

Only one caller of `validate_tree_depth`:

```
$ grep -rn validate_tree_depth includes/
